1. Title: Default of Credit Card Clients (25 January 2016)

2. Sources:
-- I-Cheng Yeh (creator)
   UCI Machine Learning Repository
   Irvine, California
   USA
-- Date: January 25, 2016
-- URL: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/350/default+of+credit+card+clients

3. Relevant Information:
   The dataset contains variables and information of 30,000 clients in Taiwan. There are variables about demographics, credit limit, payment history, bill statement and payment amounts, and whether the client defaulted. This dataset will be used to predict if clients will default on their credit card using various models.

4. Number of Instances: 30,000 (as of 25 January 2016)

5. Number of Attributes: 23 explanatory variables, 1 response variable, 1 identification variable

6. Attribute Information: 
   #   Attribute
   ------------------------
   ID: Identification Number
   X1: LIMIT_BAL - amount of given credit (Taiwan Dollars)
   X2: SEX - 1 for Male, 2 for Female
   X3: EDUCATION - 1 = graduate school; 2 = university; 3 = high school; 4 = others
   X4: MARRIAGE - 1 = married; 2 = single; 3 = others
   X5: AGE - age in years
-- X6 - X11 tracks history of past payment. -1 = pay duly; 1 = payment delay for one month; 2 = payment delay for two months
   X6: PAY_0 - repayment status in September, 2005 
   X7: PAY_2 - repayment status in August, 2005
   X8: PAY_3 - repayment status in July, 2005
   X9: PAY_4 - repayment status in June, 2005
   X10: PAY_5 - repayment status in May, 2005
   X11: PAY_6 - repayment status in April, 2005
-- X12 - X17 tracks the amount of bill statement in Taiwan Dollars
   X12: BILL_AMT1 - bill statement amount in September, 2005
   X13: BILL_AMT2 - bill statement amount in August, 2005
   X14: BILL_AMT3 - bill statement amount in July, 2005
   X15: BILL_AMT4 - bill statement amount in June, 2005
   X16: BILL_AMT5 - bill statement amount in May, 2005
   X17: BILL_AMT6 - bill statement amount in April, 2005
-- X18 - X23 tracks the amount of payment made towards a previous month's statement in Taiwan Dollars
   X18: PAY_AMT1 - payment amount made in September, 2005
   X19: PAY_AMT2 - payment amount made in August, 2005
   X20: PAY_AMT3 - payment amount made in July, 2005
   X21: PAY_AMT4 - payment amount made in June, 2005
   X22: PAY_AMT5 - payment amount made in May, 2005
   X23: PAY_AMT6 - payment amount made in April, 2005
   Y: Default payment next month - 0 = No (no default); 1 = Yes (Default)

7. Missing Attribute Values: 0

8. Class Distribution:
   No Default (0): 23,364 (77.88%)
   Default (1): 6,636 (22.12%)

9. Citation:
   Yeh, I. (2009). Default of Credit Card Clients [Dataset].
   UCI Machine Learning Repository.
   https://doi.org/10.24432/C55S3H